<article class="env-remark" id="0BNP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BNP">Remark <span data-tag="0BNP">15.92.5</span>.</a> While $R \to R_ f$ is always flat, $R \to R^\wedge $ is typically not flat unless $R$ is Noetherian (see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00MB" data-tag="00MB">10.97.2</a> and the discussion in Examples, Section <a href="/tag/0AL8" data-tag="0AL8">110.12</a>). Consequently, we cannot in general apply faithfully flat descent as discussed in Descent, Section <a href="/tag/023F" data-tag="023F">35.3</a> to the morphism $R \to R^\wedge \oplus R_ f$. Moreover, even in the Noetherian case, the usual definition of a descent datum for this morphism refers to the ring $R^\wedge \otimes _ R R^\wedge $, which we will avoid considering in this section. </p>
</article>